      "version": "12.2.0",
      "releaseDate": "2026-10-09T02:59:26Z",
      "releaseNotesUrl": "https://github.com/Dec18studios/Technically-Technicolor-DRT/releases/tag/v12.2.0",
      "releaseHighlights": "- New Preset Manager: save, update, rename, delete, import and export your own presets as .json files for Full Preset, Full Neg Preset, Neg Sensitivity, Neg Dye, Neg HD Curve, Dye Shaping and Textures\n- New Full Preset menu with four built-in looks: Modern (Single Stock + Xenon), 3 Strip (Process 4 + White Flame arc), 2 Strip (Process 3 + Carbon Arc) and 2 Strip Blue (Process 3 + Xenon). Your saved whole looks live here too\n- Preset menus now show \"(Custom)\" as soon as you change something, including when you draw curves in the Film Stock Editor\n- Auto Calibrate keeps mid grey printing neutral at your Calibration Target when you change stock, dyes or process. Works in Single Stock, Process 3 and Process 4\n- New Halation Model choice with Roadshow and Roadshow 2.0, where brighter sources glow more and the glow takes the source colour\n- New hue and amount puck in the Textures editor: drag it to set halation colour and strength in one move\n- New Grain Model choice (Classic or Emulsion), and grain no longer goes blotchy at high Grain Intensity, most noticeable on 16mm\n- Textures: new Texture Preset menu with 65mm, 35mm and 16mm formats plus Save Custom, and Edit Grain, Edit Halation and Edit MTF buttons that open that section in Single View\n- Single View now pans and zooms: drag to pan, scroll to zoom up to 20x, double-click to jump in on a spot and double-click again to go back\n- New MTF Pressure slider plus per-channel Bump Width and Fine Crispness. High Pressure no longer rings or fringes\n- New Input Primaries choice for ARRI Wide Gamut 3, DaVinci Wide Gamut, Sony S-Gamut3 and ACES AP0. Classic keeps the old behaviour\n- Carbon Arc and White Flame bulbs are rescaled to 100% brightness, so they no longer scorch highlights\n- The plugin now tells you in the inspector when an update is available\n- Fixed a crash at startup when Technicolor DRT was loaded alongside other Dec 18 plugins",
